  "summary_en": "EDPS opinion responding to the European Commission's 2020 AI White Paper. It welcomes the rights-based European approach but recommends a more nuanced risk classification, coverage of EU institutions, impact assessments, coordinated supervision, and a moratorium on remote biometric identification in public spaces.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "New AI framework should apply to Member States and EU institutions alike",
   "Regulation should protect communities and society, not only individuals",
   "Proposes a more robust, layered risk classification instead of 'high-risk or nothing'",
   "Calls for an impact assessment identifying regulatory gaps and avoiding overlapping supervisors",
   "Supports a moratorium on automated biometric recognition in public spaces"
